<details class='sub-section' id='sub_2'><summary class='sub-header'><span><span class='arrow-icon'>▶</span>03 · 逃跑、规避、侥幸逃脱与溜走 <span style='font-weight:400;font-size:0.86em;color:#cbd5e1;margin-left:8px;'>Getting away, Wriggling out & Slipping off</span></span><span class='sub-meta'>26 义项</span></summary><div class='epe-explain-box'>🎭 <b>场景认知导读：</b>拉大与追捕者的距离即逃离（get away），从束缚容器或责任中扭动钻出即逃避推脱（wriggle/weasel out of），绕着障碍物画弧线避开即规避（get around）。</div><table><tr><th width='21%'>Phrasal Verb • 语法与语域</th><th width='24%'>🎯 English Definition (WordNet)</th><th width='14%'>🔄 Single-Word Verb</th><th width='41%'>💬 Authentic Examples</th></tr>
<tr data-sep='Intransitive' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>go <span class='pt-highlight'>off</span></span><span class='sense-badge' title='该短语共有 6 个核心义项'>1/6</span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Intransitive'>🟠 不及物 (Intransitive)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：语料库日常/小说会话分布活跃 + 作为正式词 [abscond] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>run away; usually includes taking something or somebody along</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>abscond, bolt</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span>The thief made off with our silver.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>②</span>The accountant absconded with the cash from the safe.</div></div></div></td></tr>
<tr data-sep='Separable' data-reg='Neutral'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>put <span class='pt-highlight'>off</span></span><span class='sense-badge' title='该短语共有 5 个核心义项'>3/5</span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Separable'>🟢 可拆分 (v. + O + adv.)</span><span class='reg-Neutral' title='🤖 自动判定依据：语料库日常/小说会话分布活跃' style='cursor:help;'>⚖️ 通用/中性 (Neutral)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>avoid or try to avoid fulfilling, answering, or performing (duties, questions, or issues)</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>hedge, fudge</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>①</span>He dodged the issue.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>②</span>She skirted the problem.</div></div>
<div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>③</span>They tend to evade their responsibilities.</div></div></div></td></tr>
<tr data-sep='Intransitive' data-reg='Informal'><td><div class='word-line'><span class='word'>get <span class='pt-highlight'>away</span></span></div><div class='badge-stack'><span class='sep-Intransitive'>🟠 不及物 (Intransitive)</span><span class='reg-Informal' title='🤖 自动判定依据：语料库日常/小说会话分布活跃 + 作为正式词 [escape] 的日常短语替身' style='cursor:help;'>💬 口语/日常 (Informal)</span></div></td><td><span class='cn-precise' style='font-weight:600;color:#1e293b;'>run away from confinement</span></td><td><span class='eq-verb'>escape, flee</span></td><td><div class='ex-list'><div class='ex-item'><div class='ex-en'><span class='ex-num'>📌</span>The convicted murderer escaped from a high security prison.</div></div></div></td></tr>
